<section id="S4.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.1.2 </span>Language models</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct our experiments on open state-of-the-art large language models (Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.1.2 Language models ‣ 4.1 Setup ‣ 4 Experiments and Results ‣ No Answer Needed: Predicting LLM AnswerAccuracy from Question-Only Linear Probes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) varying in both training regimen and scale. We use three-shot prompting to mitigate answer formatting errors (exact prompts<span id="footnote6" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">6</span>
                
                
                
              Exploratory investigation found the specific few-shot examples to not significantly affect performance.</span></span></span> in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS8" title="A.8 Prompts ‣ Appendix A Additional results ‣ No Answer Needed: Predicting LLM AnswerAccuracy from Question-Only Linear Probes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>). The performance for each model on each dataset can be found in Table <a href="#A1.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ A.1 LLM performance on datasets ‣ Appendix A Additional results ‣ No Answer Needed: Predicting LLM AnswerAccuracy from Question-Only Linear Probes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 LLM performance on datasets ‣ Appendix A Additional results ‣ No Answer Needed: Predicting LLM AnswerAccuracy from Question-Only Linear Probes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>. Although we use a reasoning-trained model (Deepseek R1 Distill Qwen 32B), we do not employ reasoning-specific prompting and treat that identically to the other models.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S4.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Large Language Models used in our work, number of transformer layers and layer achieving the best in-distribution AUC for the direction learned on TriviaQA (Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Identifying the most discriminative layer ‣ 4 Experiments and Results ‣ No Answer Needed: Predicting LLM AnswerAccuracy from Question-Only Linear Probes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>). The first layer is 0.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S4.T2.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
