<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Assessors performance</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the gradient boosted decision tree assessors, we used XGBoost <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>. The number of trees were chosen individually for each model by performing 5-fold cross validation on the same training subset of TriviaQA as in Section <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Correctness direction generalization ‣ 4 Experiments and Results ‣ No Answer Needed: Predicting LLM AnswerAccuracy from Question-Only Linear Probes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>. The rest of XGBoost’s hyperparameters were left as default.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T7" class="ltx_table">
